  "observations": [
    "The six idle samples now visibly advance the opposed satellites through a continuous orbit with natural front and rear occlusion.",
    "Whirl ribbons reveal smoothly from the emission threshold through the mature activation landmark without a one-frame pop.",
    "The exact black and white inversion and all six character accent colors remain intact in this theme.",
    "All 25 literal eye topology families remain expressive at pet scale, including surprise rounds, slits, brushes, mixed eyes, and recovery poses.",
    "All sixteen gaze poses are semantically clear, clockwise, and free of left-right or up-down inversion.",
    "The review performance reads cleanly as surprise burst, ribbon entry, foreground storm, and a controlled return to the neutral body.",
    "No clipping, dirty transparent pixels, theme-specific geometry drift, or detached full-size effect artifacts are visible.",
    "The deliberately punchy jump, wave, failed, and travel beats remain coherent within the host's fixed four-to-eight-frame action rows."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Whirl uses a deterministic four-belt treatment rather than a stochastic trail population.",
    "The fixed Codex row budget cannot include every 60 fps intermediate frame from the motion studies.",
    "Travel rows communicate receive and write/send/dock status performances rather than literal locomotion."
  ],
